gcp_inventory.json
gcp_iam.json
gcp_schedulers.json
billing_90d.json
.venv
.superpowers/

# Archived projects keep their committed sample/reference data. The `data/`
# rule above targets the GCS-backed parquet/CSV datasets, not these fixtures —
# without this, archiving a project would silently drop them from the repo
# while leaving them on disk, so the move would read as a deletion.
!archive/**/data/
!archive/**/data/**
# ...but not files the live projects never tracked: archiving should preserve
# what was in the repo, not start committing things that were excluded.
archive/**/*.csv
# EXCEPTION, and the reason the general rule above does not fit here: these
# four Earnings Whispers exports are the ONLY copy. They are the sole input to
# scripts/match_earnings_strategy.py, the Apps Script scraper that produced
# them is archived and will not produce more, and they existed on exactly one
# disk. The rule above assumes an excluded file can be regenerated; this one
# cannot. ~700 KB total, market data only, private repo.
# Tracking them does NOT put them in a build: archive/ is excluded by both
# .gcloudignore and .dockerignore, which is a separate mechanism from git.
# Enumerated, NOT a wildcard: `*.csv` here would make any future file in this
# directory trackable, so a routine `git add .` could commit unrelated or
# sensitive CSV data straight past the archive/**/*.csv policy above.
!archive/google-apps-script/data/reference/Stocks from Earnings Whisper - Bull Spreads.csv
!archive/google-apps-script/data/reference/Stocks from Earnings Whisper - Covered Calls.csv
!archive/google-apps-script/data/reference/Stocks from Earnings Whisper - Long Calls.csv
!archive/google-apps-script/data/reference/Stocks from Earnings Whisper - Long Calls(1).csv
archive/**/.clasp.json
# ...and never secrets: git takes the LAST matching rule, so the broad
# negation above would otherwise override the repo-wide sensitive-file
# excludes for anything under archive/**/data/ — a credentials file dropped
# beside the fixtures would become stageable by a routine `git add .`.
# Re-apply the patterns from the top of this file for the archived subtree.
archive/**/.env
archive/**/.env.*
archive/**/credentials/
archive/**/*.key
archive/**/*-credentials.json
archive/**/.gcp-key.json
